<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Billiton to supply alumina to Mozal smelter.</title>
<headline>Billiton to supply alumina to Mozal smelter.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Gencor Ltd said on Tuesday its Billiton unit would supply alumina to the new 245,000-tonne-a-year Mozal primary aluminium smelter in southern Mozambique from Australia, Brazil or Surinam.</p>
<p>Rob Barbour, managing director of the company's existing South African aluminium business, Alusaf, told reporters material would come from Billiton refineries in these origins in order to ensure consistent quality.</p>
<p>Billiton, which Gencor plans to list in London, already supplies alumina to Alusaf's smelters at Bayside and Hillside.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
